many upcoming high-profile films have  already scheduled their debuts and some  have even released trailers to the  public at large unfortunately some of  them also look pretty lame you heard it  here first  these are fated to be the worst movies  of 2019 all the most popular stage  musicals eventually get adapted into  films they're well known enough for  studios to take a chance on them they  almost always score an Oscar nom or two  and they give musical fans who don't  live in New York a rare chance to enjoy  them in 2019 another well-known musical  will hit movie screens and no sadly it's  not Hamilton it's cats debuting on  Broadway in 1982 Katz is a loosely  plotted show based on a book of poetry  by TS Eliot which is about well cats  singing dancing frolicking homeless cats  cats his original run ended in 2000 and  Hollywood has finally figured out a way  to do this show but not via animation  like you might expect no it seems the  stars of the movie who include Taylor  Swift Ian McKellen Jennifer Hudson and  James Corden are going to actually dress  up in cat costumes so does this have any  prayer of being the next musical to  clean up at the Oscars not meow  not ever it just wouldn't be a New Year  without another movie in which an angry  Liam Neeson tracks and kills a small  army of bad guys who did him wrong  following the three taken movies run all  night the commuter and many many more  comes cold pursuit  this time Neeson shows off his very  particular set of skills as a  mild-mannered rocky mountain snow plow  driver named Nelson who is forced into  action when his son is killed by a drug  cartel  unfortunately Neeson has done the same  movie so many times that it's starting  to get a little embarrassing why would I  do it  because there would be a reward  one thing in cold pursuits favor however  is that it's based on a pretty good  Norwegian dark comedy called in order of  disappearance it's just a shame they  seem to have drained all the humor out  of it in the beachbum the always cool  and totally chill Matthew McConaughey  plays a beach loving stoner named moon  dog and no despite what you might  remember this movie doesn't already  exist maybe you're thinking of surfer  dude while the title and details make it  sound like a straight-to-video National  Lampoon branded boorish comedy from the  early 90s it's actually an indie movie  albeit one directed by Harmony Korine  mostly known for more unsettling  projects such as kids and Gummo at least  the cast is likable Zac Efron plays a  dude named flicker Snoop Dogg portrays  someone genuinely named lingerie and  Martin Lawrence makes an appearance as  Captain whack role on awards season the  Rambo movies may hold claim to the film  franchise that has feared the furthest  from its original intent the first entry  in the series first blood was the  harrowing and tragic story of a PTSD  stricken Vietnam War veteran starring  Sylvester Stallone in what was probably  his finest and most nuanced work since  the original Rocky  then came the second one and everything  changed war won't stop a First Blood  Part two it will escalate to Rambo 3  which should really be called rainbow 2  First Blood Part 3 but the Rambo titles  never made sense the political climate  of the 1980s fueled an explosion of  action movies that celebrated American  patriotism and hardcore violence and so  the subsequent first blood sequels had  the same broken man become a  muscle-bound machine gun wielding  one-man army who routinely shoots up  entire villages full of terrorists live  for nothing  but for something Stallone's career has  been reinvigorated in recent years  thanks to the success of old-school  action franchise The Expendables as well  as his Oscar nomination for the role of  Rocky Balboa and Creed as part of this  victory lap Stallone has decided to go  and make the completely unnecessary  Rambo 5 this time Rambo faces off  against the drug cartel odds are he'll  come out on top which is an impressive  feat considering both Stallone and his  character are well over 70 years old the  rhythm section is pretty much exactly  like peppermint 2008 teens moderately  successful taken rip-off starring  Jennifer Garner  this one stars Gossip Girl veteran Blake  Lively at Stefanie Patrick a woman who  slowly and methodically tracks down a  bunch of bad guys because she just knows  they're responsible for the plane crash  that killed her family Lively is no  stranger to an action thriller having  starred in 2016's the shallows but it's  hard to get worked up about this and the  best part it's based on a book series so  you can probably count on a sequel or  six somewhere down the line  [Music]
 

